# Caddy reverse proxy for the dashboard Tailscale HTTPS path.
#
# Topology:
#   Remote user → HTTPS → Tailscale Serve (on the M5 / HTTPS endpoint host)
#     → HTTP → 10.10.10.2:8444 (this proxy on the M1, bound to private Ethernet only)
#       → HTTP → dashboard:8080 (via dashboard-tls-proxy Docker network)
#
# Tailscale Serve runs on the M5 (10.10.10.1), not on the M1. It terminates
# TLS and forwards plain HTTP over the direct Ethernet link to this Caddy
# container on the M1 (10.10.10.2). The M1's Caddy then reverse-proxies to
# the dashboard container on the internal Docker network.
#
# The proxy forces X-Forwarded-Proto: https so the dashboard sets the
# Secure cookie flag. The dashboard trusts this proxy's fixed source IP
# (172.28.0.2) on the internal Docker network.
#
# Security boundary:
#   - Port 8444 is published only on 10.10.10.2 (private direct Ethernet).
#   - Normal LAN clients (192.168.68.x) cannot reach this listener.
#   - The dashboard's published port 192.168.68.68:8088 is on the default
#     bridge network; LAN clients appear as the Docker bridge gateway IP,
#     which is NOT in the trusted proxy list.

:8444 {
	reverse_proxy dashboard:8080 {
		header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
	}
}
